# Button Interaction Feedback

- Every button and button-like control must have a visually distinct hover state on devices that support hover.
- Every button must provide immediate pressed feedback on click or tap, such as a subtle scale, tint, elevation, or shadow change.
- Hover and pressed effects must not shift the surrounding layout or reduce text readability.
- Keep a clear `:focus-visible` state for keyboard users; hover must never be the only interaction cue.
- Disabled controls must not show hover or pressed feedback and must look unavailable.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences when an effect uses animation or movement.
- Verify these states whenever a button is added or visually changed.
